## SQ-PST-09c | Vinery grass slab slower in winter, rerun on the direct hook (2026-11-17)
@group A (same temperate column)
@commands Rule (changelog 1.2.02, CropSeasons GRASS): grass-type spread is off in winter only (`[crop_seasons] grassOffPenalty` 0.5 of the tries refused), neutral in spring, summer, autumn and in wet/dry biomes (crops.md "Grasses" still says summer/wet/dry: writeup stale). As SQ-PST-03 with a 32x32 pad of `vinery:dirt_slab` (bottom) ringed with `vinery:grass_slab`; count with `/fill <pad> vinery:dirt_slab replace vinery:grass_slab`; then put stone on one grass slab in summer and wait 30 s (it still turns to a dirt slab); 3 runs each in `mid_spring`, `mid_summer`, `mid_winter` at randomTickSpeed 100, rebuilding the pad before each run; reset to 3. Boot log: `[creativecalendar] grass season hook live: <target>` once for this block
@pass winter mean about 50 % of spring (35 to 85 %: pad saturation pulls it up; the shell line's range); the hook-live line present
@fails no hook-live line: the Vinery port's `SpreadableGrassSlabBlock.randomTick` does not call `GrassSeasonHook.refuse` (Calendar's `VineryGrassSlabSeasonMixin` was deleted 2026-11-17, plan_rules_fixes.md 12f step 1; Creative Brewing and Calendar jars of 2026-11-17 both needed); the covered slab not dying: the hook placed before the survive check
@jars creativecalendar creativebrewing
@reviewed 2026-11-20
